                "lastName": "Kuriloff"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "The members of an organization possess experience and skill that are too often neglected by management. These dormant resources can be released as management develops facility in communicating with the individuals who make up the organization, singly and in groups. To improve organizational effectiveness, communication must be aimed at improving both interpersonal competence and technical competence. Management must deal with both the feelings of human beings and their ideas.",
