            }
        ],
        "abstract": "Most university curricula in engineering are seriously deficient in training in the techniques of communication. Consequently, most engineers are poor communicators because they have never been taught the proper techniques of speaking, listening, and writing. This paper calls attention to several communication problems; shades of meaning, background experience, sophisticated language, and vocabulary limitations are considered. Suggestions are made for the improvement of these areas.",
